## Authentication

`config/SecurityConfig` requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every route under `/api/v1`;
`/health`{{if .Observability}} and `/metrics`{{end}} stay public. Tokens are HS256 JWTs with `sub` and `exp`, signed
with `JWT_SECRET` by your identity service. Controllers read the caller with
`@AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt` (see `MeController`). `ServerTests` shows how to sign a test token.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Observability}}

## Metrics and tracing

`GET /metrics` serves Micrometer metrics (`http_server_requests_seconds`, JVM, ...) for Prometheus.
Requests are traced with OpenTelemetry; logs carry `trace_id` and `span_id`, and spans are exported
when `TRACING_EXPORT_ENABLED=true`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}

## Cache

`config/CacheConfig` enables Spring's cache on Redis: annotate a method with
`@Cacheable("products")` to cache its result. `/health` pings Redis too.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Migrations}}

## Migrations

Flyway applies `src/main/resources/db/migration/V<n>__<name>.sql` on start, in version order,
and records them in `flyway_schema_history`. Add a new file for every change; never edit an applied one.

Test them against a throwaway database:

```bash
TEST_DATABASE_URL=jdbc:... TEST_DATABASE_USER=... TEST_DATABASE_PASSWORD=... ./mvnw verify
```
{{- end}}

## Logging

Log4j 2 (Logback is excluded) writes JSON with snake_case fields: `@timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `service`, `env`, `request_id`, `logger`.
`RequestIdFilter` puts `request_id` in the ThreadContext for each request and clears it afterwards.
Keep `message` constant and put dynamic values in their own fields:

```java
try (var ctx = CloseableThreadContext.put("order_id", id)) {
    LOG.info("order created");
}
```

Log an error once, at the boundary, with the exception: `LOG.error("payment failed", e);`.
Never log passwords, tokens, API keys or personal data.
